# Use Case Diagram

```mermaid
useCaseDiagram
    package "Bhuk Food Delivery System" {
        actor Customer
        actor "Restaurant Staff" as Staff
        actor "Delivery Partner" as Partner
        actor Administrator
        actor "Payment Gateway" as Payment

        usecase "UC-01: Browse Menu" as UC1
        usecase "UC-02: Manage Cart" as UC2
        usecase "UC-03: Place Order" as UC3
        usecase "UC-04: Track Order" as UC4
        usecase "UC-05: View Order History" as UC5
        usecase "UC-06: Manage Addresses" as UC6
        usecase "UC-07: Login/Register" as UC7

        usecase "UC-08: Process Orders" as UC8
        usecase "UC-09: Update Order Status" as UC9
        usecase "UC-10: View Order Queue" as UC10

        usecase "UC-11: Accept Delivery" as UC11
        usecase "UC-12: Update Location" as UC12
        usecase "UC-13: Mark Picked Up" as UC13
        usecase "UC-14: Mark Delivered" as UC14
        usecase "UC-15: Report Issue" as UC15
        usecase "UC-16: Set Availability" as UC16

        usecase "UC-17: Manage Menu" as UC17
        usecase "UC-18: Manage Users" as UC18
        usecase "UC-19: Manage Outlets" as UC19
        usecase "UC-20: View Reports" as UC20
        usecase "UC-21: Assign Roles" as UC21

        usecase "UC-22: Process Payment" as UC22
        usecase "UC-23: Payment Webhook" as UC23
    }

    Customer --> UC1
    Customer --> UC2
    Customer --> UC3
    Customer --> UC4
    Customer --> UC5
    Customer --> UC6
    Customer --> UC7

    Staff --> UC8
    Staff --> UC9
    Staff --> UC10

    Partner --> UC11
    Partner --> UC12
    Partner --> UC13
    Partner --> UC14
    Partner --> UC15
    Partner --> UC16

    Administrator --> UC17
    Administrator --> UC18
    Administrator --> UC19
    Administrator --> UC20
    Administrator --> UC21

    Payment --> UC22
    Payment --> UC23

    UC3 --> UC22 : <<include>>
    UC8 ..> UC11 : <<extend>> (when READY_FOR_PICKUP)
```